Subject: [PATCH] the guild advertisements are pruned from bot speech

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Four suggest_something rows of ai_playerbot_texts (ids 741, 743, 801
and 816 in data/sql/playerbots/base/ai_playerbot_texts.sql at the pin
below) are guild searches: "%my_role is looking for guild." and three
like it. A bot already in a guild that says one asserts a state it is
not in. Patch 0017 took suggest_something out of the guild channel; the
rows still play in world and general chat.

The prune was first merged as an SQL file in the site's repository
(its #1640 and #2252), where nothing applies it: the realm build
compiles this tree plus these patches, and the module runs its own
database updater over data/sql/playerbots/updates/ in this tree
(src/Script/Playerbots.cpp, ModuleDBUpdater::Update, gated on
Playerbots.Updates.EnableDatabases, default on). This patch adds the
update file there, so the next start of a worldserver built with it
deletes the four rows once and records the file as applied.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream (or the operator's fork) removing or rewriting those four rows
in its own seed or updates.

APPLIES TO

mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130 (the pin
patch 0017 names), on top of local patches 0001-0024. Adds one new file,
data/sql/playerbots/updates/2026_11_12_00_ai_playerbot_guild_ads.sql,
which sorts after the pin's last update
(2026_10_05_01_ai_playerbot_rpg_gather_texts.sql). Touches no source.

diff --git a/data/sql/playerbots/updates/2026_11_12_00_ai_playerbot_guild_ads.sql b/data/sql/playerbots/updates/2026_11_12_00_ai_playerbot_guild_ads.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4603333
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/sql/playerbots/updates/2026_11_12_00_ai_playerbot_guild_ads.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+-- Prune the guild advertisements from the suggest_something speech class
+-- (mod-overseer patch 0025).
+--
+-- These four seed rows of ai_playerbot_texts each say the speaker is looking
+-- for a guild, which is false for a bot already in one:
+--
+--   id 741: %my_role is looking for guild.
+--   id 743: %my_role wants to join a good guild.
+--   id 801: any guilds willing to carry %my_role?
+--   id 816: any leveling guilds out there?
+--
+-- Delete rather than rewrite: each row carries the same guild search in its
+-- localized columns. ai_playerbot_texts_chance is keyed by class name, so
+-- nothing is orphaned. Each delete is guarded to the suggest_something class.
+DELETE FROM `ai_playerbot_texts`
+WHERE `name` = 'suggest_something'
+  AND `id` IN (741, 743, 801, 816);
